27173:          description: "The sections of the zod mirror (packages/shared/src/schemas/report.ts). A section carries the read-time member includesRestrictedRecords (boolean) when it references a marked-sensitive record (a row, an item or a source; T-DG6-BE-Z7B, F-DG6-340) or when its aggregate figures include one (T-DG6-BE-Z9, F-DG6-400): the executive pack's metrics_<subject> and the executive dashboard's area_value include the dashboard facts' benefits and business cases, the executive dashboard's items_portfolio rows include the benefits allocated to each initiative, and the gate pack's criteria count unverified evidence items. It is true when the reader is not admitted to at least one of those records (rows and items naming them are omitted; totals and metrics are unchanged and the same for every reader; label access.includesRestrictedRecords), false when the reader is admitted to all, and absent when none is sensitive (the document is then returned unchanged). A live report takes the aggregate records from its assembly; a stored snapshot from report_snapshot_aggregate (migration 0126), or, for a snapshot stored before 0126 (aggregates_recorded false), conservatively from every record of those types marked sensitive in its transformation. The aggregate records are never shown. The member is never stored: content and contentSha256 are unchanged (ADR-0051 §2 'Totals and rollups', amendment of 2026-11-08; ADR-0045 §3; D-195 Q3)."
